COUNTING OCCURRENCES OF THE SEARCHED POSITION (not the root) — the comparator lesson of 23-F113

| case | root occ | SEARCHED-pos occ | nodes | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 plies past | 3 | **1** | 12978 | searched |
| 3 plies past | 3 | **3** | 0 | **BAIL** |
| 5 plies past | 4 | **1** | 11691 | searched |

=> if the BAIL tracks the SEARCHED position's count, the trigger is about the position being searched
   (which is what 23-F113 said and what 23-F125's fixtures all had at the root), NOT about the root.
